  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "For $\\triangle ABC$ we are given that $\\angle A=45^{\\circ}$, $a=\\sqrt{18}$ and $c=5$. Find $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$b=\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{22}}{2}$ or $b=\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{22}}{2}$.\n\nApply the cosine rule and solve the resulting quadratic.",
      "worked": "Using the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2&=b^2+c^2-2bc\\cos A\\\\18&=b^2+25-10b\\cos45^{\\circ}\\\\18&=b^2+25-5\\sqrt{2}\\,b\\\\0&=b^2-5\\sqrt{2}\\,b+7\\\\b&=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}\\pm\\sqrt{(5\\sqrt{2})^2-4(1)(7)}}{2}\\\\b&=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}\\pm\\sqrt{22}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are positive and give valid triangles.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
